==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s (4,000%) spawn, delay 1~6 seconds<sup>30f~180f</sup>.
*100 [[Mooth]]s spawn, delay 1~6 seconds<sup>30f~180f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Squire Rel]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 1~6 seconds<sup>30f~180f</sup>.
**25 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 0.33~2 seconds<sup>10f~60f</sup>.
**1 [[M. Ost]] spawns.
**1 [[M. Ost]] spawns.
**1 [[M. Ost]] spawns.

==Strategy==
A difficult stage on paper, very straightforward in reality. One would think that 3 M. Osts at the same time would be incredibly hard to stall, if it wasn't for the fact that the stage gives free money in the form of 100 relatively unbuffed Mooths. You can be assured that it is impossible to run out of money in this stage. You are free to bring as many anti Relic units as you like, particularly Crowd controllers like [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]] or Area attackers such as [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapsticks]], and, on higher crowns, [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]] or [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]]. You should bring anti relic meatshields such as [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Future Cat]] or at least 4 [[Meatshield class Cats|meatshields]]. Research combos are recommended to improve the efficiency of both meatshields and attackers.
Crowd control Ubers that target all traits will prove useful here even if they are not curse immune, so long as they can outrange the M. Osts.

